<section class="tk-res"><div class="tk-shell">
<div class="tk-res-hero"><div><span class="tk-ip-kicker">TRACEKIT RESOURCES</span><h1>Better questions.<br><em>Clearer answers.</em></h1><p>Learn how acquisition, attribution, commerce, and financial records connect. Explore practical guides, investigate common reporting challenges, and find your next step with TraceKit.</p><a class="btn" href="#tk-res-guides">Explore the Guides ↓</a></div><div class="tk-res-hero-panel"><span class="tk-res-panel-label">START HERE / 3 STEPS</span><h2>Make sense of your business data.</h2><div><b>01</b><span><strong>Connect the sources</strong><small>Understand which records are available.</small></span></div><div><b>02</b><span><strong>Follow the relationships</strong><small>Keep identities and events distinct.</small></span></div><div><b>03</b><span><strong>Investigate the evidence</strong><small>See what matches—and what doesn't.</small></span></div></div></div>
<div class="tk-res-featured"><div><span class="tk-ip-kicker">FEATURED RESOURCE</span><h2>From click to customer to dollar.</h2><p>See how a single customer journey can connect campaign activity, purchases, upsells, rebills, and refunds while preserving source evidence.</p><span class="tk-res-featured-note">Includes an interactive illustrative journey, not live customer data.</span></div><a class="btn" href="/pages/customer-journeys">Explore Customer Journeys →</a></div>
<div id="tk-res-guides" class="tk-res-heading"><span class="tk-ip-kicker">THE LEARNING LIBRARY</span><h2>Explore the concepts behind TraceKit.</h2><p>Six practical guides you can read right here. Choose a topic or search for what matters to your team.</p></div>
<div class="tk-res-toolbar"><label for="tk-res-search">Search resources<input id="tk-res-search" type="search" placeholder="Search topics or questions..." autocomplete="off"></label><div class="tk-res-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter resources"><button type="button" class="is-active" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All guides</button><button type="button" data-filter="attribution" aria-pressed="false">Attribution</button><button type="button" data-filter="journeys" aria-pressed="false">Journeys</button><button type="button" data-filter="reconciliation" aria-pressed="false">Reconciliation</button><button type="button" data-filter="financial" aria-pressed="false">Financial</button><button type="button" data-filter="intelligence" aria-pressed="false">Intelligence</button><button type="button" data-filter="integrations" aria-pressed="false">Integrations</button></div></div>
<div class="tk-res-guides"><article class="tk-res-guide" data-category="attribution" data-search="attribution & identity how a click becomes a defensible attribution link learn why a provider click id, an order reference, and a customer identifier answer different questions—and how deterministic relationships help connect them."><div class="tk-res-guide-top"><span>01 / Attribution & Identity</span><span class="tk-res-guide-type">PRACTICAL GUIDE</span></div><h3>How a click becomes a defensible attribution link</h3><p>Learn why a provider click ID, an order reference, and a customer identifier answer different questions—and how deterministic relationships help connect them.</p><details><summary>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></summary><div class="tk-res-guide-body"><strong>The source of a conversion is not necessarily the cause of a business outcome.</strong><p>Capture original click and transaction identifiers, keep attribution identity separate from commerce identity, and prefer exact provider or shared references. When a relationship cannot be established, retain the unmatched record for investigation.</p></div></details></article>
<article class="tk-res-guide" data-category="journeys" data-search="customer journeys what happens after the first purchase? understand how upsells, subscriptions, rebills, refunds, and disputes contribute to a customer's commercial story."><div class="tk-res-guide-top"><span>02 / Customer Journeys</span><span class="tk-res-guide-type">PRACTICAL GUIDE</span></div><h3>What happens after the first purchase?</h3><p>Understand how upsells, subscriptions, rebills, refunds, and disputes contribute to a customer's commercial story.</p><details><summary>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></summary><div class="tk-res-guide-body"><strong>A customer journey is a collection of related events, not a single flattened order.</strong><p>Preserve distinct event records and connect them using supported parent-child or exact transaction references. Keep financial adjustments separate so later refunds and disputes do not silently rewrite the original sale.</p></div></details></article>
<article class="tk-res-guide" data-category="reconciliation" data-search="reconciliation why two dashboards show different numbers a practical framework for investigating mismatched conversions, orders, payment records, and financial adjustments."><div class="tk-res-guide-top"><span>03 / Reconciliation</span><span class="tk-res-guide-type">PRACTICAL GUIDE</span></div><h3>Why two dashboards show different numbers</h3><p>A practical framework for investigating mismatched conversions, orders, payment records, and financial adjustments.</p><details><summary>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></summary><div class="tk-res-guide-body"><strong>A discrepancy is a finding to investigate, not a reason to overwrite source data.</strong><p>Compare the same reporting window, currencies, time zones, event types, and source IDs. Identify missing or duplicated records and retain raw provider evidence before applying normalization or reconciliation rules.</p></div></details></article>
<article class="tk-res-guide" data-category="financial" data-search="profit & financial outcomes revenue isn't the same as profit explore how advertising costs, processing, fulfillment, refunds, and disputes affect the financial picture."><div class="tk-res-guide-top"><span>04 / Profit & Financial Outcomes</span><span class="tk-res-guide-type">PRACTICAL GUIDE</span></div><h3>Revenue isn't the same as profit</h3><p>Explore how advertising costs, processing, fulfillment, refunds, and disputes affect the financial picture.</p><details><summary>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></summary><div class="tk-res-guide-body"><strong>Gross sales, collected revenue, and net profit are different measurements.</strong><p>Start with distinct commerce events, account for actual adjustments, and subtract supported cost categories only when the relevant data is available. Mark missing costs rather than reporting an unsupported profit number.</p></div></details></article>
<article class="tk-res-guide" data-category="intelligence" data-search="tracekit intelligence from a business question to supporting evidence see how built-in intelligence can help investigate relationships while keeping uncertainty visible."><div class="tk-res-guide-top"><span>05 / TraceKit Intelligence</span><span class="tk-res-guide-type">PRACTICAL GUIDE</span></div><h3>From a business question to supporting evidence</h3><p>See how built-in Intelligence can help investigate relationships while keeping uncertainty visible.</p><details><summary>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></summary><div class="tk-res-guide-body"><strong>A useful answer should be traceable to its underlying records.</strong><p>Begin with a specific question, inspect the available source relationships, and distinguish verified links from unresolved evidence. Available Intelligence tools and actions depend on account permissions and production readiness.</p></div></details></article>
<article class="tk-res-guide" data-category="integrations" data-search="integrations & mcp connecting systems without losing context understand the difference between supported data connections and optional access from compatible external ai assistants."><div class="tk-res-guide-top"><span>06 / Integrations & MCP</span><span class="tk-res-guide-type">PRACTICAL GUIDE</span></div><h3>Connecting systems without losing context</h3><p>Understand the difference between supported data connections and optional access from compatible external AI assistants.</p><details><summary>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></summary><div class="tk-res-guide-body"><strong>An ecosystem listing does not guarantee a live connector or every possible operation.</strong><p>Confirm a connector's supported sources, permissions, sync scope, and readiness before relying on it. MCP provides governed access to supported capabilities where enabled; it is not required to use built-in TraceKit Intelligence.</p></div></details></article></div><p class="tk-res-empty" hidden>No resources match your search. Try another keyword or category.</p>
<div class="tk-res-heading"><span class="tk-ip-kicker">GO DEEPER</span><h2>Explore TraceKit.</h2><p>Continue with the product areas and documentation relevant to your work.</p></div>
